Wolfgang Loske (wloske@x.cip.e-technik.uni-erlangen.de) wrote:
: But my question(s) follows:

: 1) What the hell are named weapons and what do they do.
:    All the experienced people are talking about Mjollnir and Stormbringer and
:    other neat things as they were the most common things. I just browsed
:    through 33 Dlvls and never found something like that.

In stories and legends there have always been swords with specific names
Excalibur is King Arthur's sword
Stormbringer is Elric's sword (from stories by Micheal Moorcock)
Mjollnir is Thor's (as in the Norse God) Hammer
Fire Brand and Frost Brand come from the RPG Dungeons and Dragons
Vorpal Blade is also from D&D.

There are others.  Basically they are swords of remarkable extra power.
For example Stormbringer drains the life from your opponents.  Excalibur
has a bunch of subtle powers.  Vorpal Blade has a chance to kill your
opponent instantly by chopping of its head.

There are a few ways to obtain a named weapon:
1) Name it yourself (Sting and Orcrist only)
2) Dip a long sword into a fountain (this yields Excalibur, only for
   Lawful characters and you should only try when you have gained several
   levels)
3) If you sacrafice enough monsters to your god, the god might grant you
a weapon.
4) You can wish for one.  Let me know if you need the exact wordings of
my favorite weapons.

